#: ../../source/docs/setting-up-for-tuning.rst:4
#: 8bc805ed83eb4eac9856e3dc50ad445d
msgid "Setting the Aircraft Up for Tuning"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/setting-up-for-tuning.rst:6
#: 6f27881157ce4f9693d388044f7ca547
msgid "The following parameters should be set correctly based on the specifications of your aircraft. Each one impacts the quality of the tuning process."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/setting-up-for-tuning.rst:10
#: 4c19eca5dde048d69e769ea62af07dc6
msgid "Battery setting"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/setting-up-for-tuning.rst:11
#: f3658322cc474283931c8765ad10161e
msgid "It is very important to ensure that the thrust curve of your VTOL motors is as linear as possible. A linear thrust curve means that changes in the actual thrust produced by a motor is directly proportional to the thrust being demanded by ArduPilot. If your thrust curve is badly non-linear then you will never produce a good tune, and in some cases may end up with such a bad tune that your vehicle can become completely unstable and crash."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/setting-up-for-tuning.rst:19
#: 21787cfe19cb4d7788119410745eb976
msgid "There are 3 common causes of a non-linear thrust curve."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/setting-up-for-tuning.rst:21
#: b351013732044fbe9bfb67d4d4c4348e
msgid "voltage sag as throttle is increased."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/setting-up-for-tuning.rst:22
#: 5d8e5925f238416db2200319dd404660
msgid "incorrect end-point setup in the PWM range you use to your ESCs (see \"Motors setup\" below)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/setting-up-for-tuning.rst:23
#: 25e7fe5b16b1411aa70fad6710bfc7c2
msgid "non-linearity in the thrust produced by your propeller, ESC and motor combination"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/setting-up-for-tuning.rst:25
#: 214a452ae6834bec949206430d7419ac
msgid "Start with setting up the voltage range to cope with voltage sag. Parameters used to linearise your motor thrust curve."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/setting-up-for-tuning.rst:28
#: 0d6ac88a8ac94dc782ddd7d453c84bc6
msgid ":ref:`MOT_BAT_VOLT_MAX <MOT_BAT_VOLT_MAX>` should be set to the maximum voltage of your batteries, e.g. 4.2v x No. Cells for standard LiPos, or as appropriate if using a different battery type."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/setting-up-for-tuning.rst:29
#: 34b520bb33c24c45b67715ddf7629b05
msgid ":ref:`MOT_BAT_VOLT_MIN <MOT_BAT_VOLT_MIN>` should be set to the minimum voltage of your batteries, e.g. 3.3v x No. Cells for standard LiPos, or as appropriate if using a different battery type ."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/setting-up-for-tuning.rst:30
#: 502d1a6dad574f9e8f89da8746d28d1d
msgid ":ref:`MOT_OPTIONS<MOT_OPTIONS>` = 0 (default). The default is to use sag compensated voltage for the above and during tuning computations. It can be set to 1 to use raw voltage instead of sag compensated voltage, which may improve tuning results for light vehicles."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/setting-up-for-tuning.rst:32
#: 92fdbf1628904383bbe8ac136d206b7f
msgid "Next setup the thrust expo. If you are setting up a professional aircraft then you should invest in a thrust stand so you can accurately measure the true thrust for your motor/ESC/propeller combination as you vary the throttle. Then you will adjust the expo value along with the endpoints (given by motors setup below) so that the thrust between the endpoints is as linear as possible. Do not trust manufacturer data for the thrust curve as they are frequently inaccurate. See :ref:`motor-thrust-scaling` for details on thrust scaling."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/setting-up-for-tuning.rst:38
#: 9ce68a72fba84286b6e64c6db5f8d900
msgid "If you are setting up a hobby grade vehicle then you can use the graph below to estimate the correct :ref:`MOT_THST_EXPO <MOT_THST_EXPO>` value for your aircraft."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/setting-up-for-tuning.rst:40
#: f17c0eeadfaf4ba78d39d5958730d396
msgid ":ref:`MOT_THST_EXPO <MOT_THST_EXPO>`: 0.55 for 5 inch props, 0.65 for 10 inch props, 0.75 for 20 inch props  (or larger). This parameter should be derived by thrust stand measurements for best results (don’t trust manufacturer data)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/setting-up-for-tuning.rst:46
#: ac979fc90ef54235b226a2577d036f13
msgid "Motors setup"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/setting-up-for-tuning.rst:48
#: 01b2c58d148c4451a58ffddd92d95555
msgid "The motor parameters define the PWM output range sent to the ESCs. This is critical to ensure that the entire range of throttle values used in flight is within the linear range of your propulsion system."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/setting-up-for-tuning.rst:53
#: 39490c3a026541f1ae9e8a4588f8468e
msgid "Parameters used to define the output range sent to the ESC."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/setting-up-for-tuning.rst:55
#: ad3819cff38f438ea2875a8420bec5a1
msgid ":ref:`MOT_PWM_MAX <MOT_PWM_MAX>`: Check ESC manual for fixed range or 2000us"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/setting-up-for-tuning.rst:56
#: d921d28ae08643429bd7809b38d1cf39
msgid ":ref:`MOT_PWM_MIN <MOT_PWM_MIN>`: Check ESC manual for fixed range or 1000us"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/setting-up-for-tuning.rst:57
#: 7740718dbb004505af386d006e17f6ea
msgid ":ref:`MOT_SPIN_ARM <MOT_SPIN_ARM>`: use the :ref:`motor test feature <connect-escs-and-motors_testing_motor_spin_directions>` to determine a value which will reliably start the motors spinning at a low rpm as an indication of the armed state."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/setting-up-for-tuning.rst:58
#: 138713cefa424be0afc514787e61c93b
msgid ":ref:`MOT_SPIN_MAX <MOT_SPIN_MAX>`: 0.95"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/setting-up-for-tuning.rst:59
#: 4161c0d047af48f9bfc46263246dd6c6
msgid ":ref:`MOT_SPIN_MIN <MOT_SPIN_MIN>`: use the :ref:`motor test feature <connect-escs-and-motors_testing_motor_spin_directions>` and motor test data, if available, to set the lower range of linear thrust. The default value is usually adequate for hobby uses."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/setting-up-for-tuning.rst:60
#: e654c95c7dcf42008066f1459efa0f85
msgid ":ref:`MOT_THST_HOVER <MOT_THST_HOVER>`: 0.25 or below the expected actual hover thrust percentage (lower is safe)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/setting-up-for-tuning.rst:63
#: 0f581f70b2ef42b9a4060ee9b29cd6d7
msgid "PID Controller Initial Setup"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/setting-up-for-tuning.rst:65
#: 468c7af8b65a434a9e4902434f531d2d
msgid "The settings below are meant to get your PID controller acceleration and filter settings into the right approximate range for your vehicle. These parameters are critical to the tuning process. The PID controller default values for axis P/D/I values are usually safe for first test hovers of most vehicles."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/setting-up-for-tuning.rst:70
#: a2ddf3d14bb740f78bb3c1e0bcfbf6bf
msgid ":ref:`INS_ACCEL_FILTER <INS_ACCEL_FILTER>`:  10Hz"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/setting-up-for-tuning.rst:71
#: e366fb0c942f4290accd4914e4551545
msgid ":ref:`INS_GYRO_FILTER <INS_GYRO_FILTER>`: 80Hz for 5 inch props, 40Hz for 10 inch props, 20Hz for 20 inch props (or larger)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/setting-up-for-tuning.rst:72
#: 95999fc136fe4f43848fee4579380cc2
msgid ":ref:`ATC_ACC_P_MAX<ATC_ACC_P_MAX>`: 1100 for 10 inch props, 500 for 20 inch props, 200 for 30 inch props"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/setting-up-for-tuning.rst:73
#: 0781f4f4d2ba4d72a303f70f6343000b
msgid ":ref:`ATC_ACC_R_MAX<ATC_ACC_R_MAX>`: 1100 for 10 inch props, 500 for 20 inch props, 200 for 30 inch props"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/setting-up-for-tuning.rst:74
#: 6e24d439e363465dad77e3469843164b
msgid ":ref:`ATC_ACC_Y_MAX<ATC_ACC_Y_MAX>`: 200 for 10 inch props, 100 for 20 inch props, 90 for 30 inch props"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/setting-up-for-tuning.rst:75
#: 973a512503464ec0a8b7a91b7aa731f1
msgid ":ref:`ATC_RAT_PIT_FLTD <ATC_RAT_PIT_FLTD__AC_AttitudeControl_Multi>`: :ref:`INS_GYRO_FILTER <INS_GYRO_FILTER>` / 2"
msgstr ""

